    "media:imagetext": "Manila\nSunday, November 23, 1952\nDear Femily,\nWe've had a busy time in Manila since our arrival lest\nMonday afternoon. Our plans are sufficiently jelled now to permit\nof en itinerary which we hope cen be followed. It follows:\nPAA 2\nLV Menile\nAR Honolulu\nLV Honolulu\nAR San Francisco\nLV San Francisco\nAR Houston\nLV Houston\nAR St. Louis\nLV St. Louis\nAR Louisville\nLV Louisville\nAR New York\n11/27\n9:00 PM\n11/28\n4:15 AM\n12/4\n7:30\nPM\n12/5\n6:45 AM\n12/6\n1:15 PM\n32/6\n10:55 PM\n12/8\n3:00 PM\n12/8\n5:45 PM\n12/11\n5:25\nPM\n12/11\n7:10\nPM\n12/14 11:00 AM\n12/14 4:22 PM\nPAA 842\nAAL/CAL 954\nC\u0026S 600\nEAL 454\nEAL 450\nWe are both looking forward to this last lap in our trip\naround the world, especially our stops at Houston, St. Louis and\nLouisville.\nOrdinarily weld look forward to that projected stay et\nHonolulu but I honestly think if it weren't for some business there\nthet we'd gallop right throush.\nDebby has been overseas since Sept-\nember 5th living out of a suitcase, weering the same dresses, sleeping\nin strange places end eating food which, with the exception of Paris\nand Switzerland has not always been too good. I had one week at home\nin October so it's that much easier for me.\nHowever, Debby found\nan old rilipino shell collector here which is for her what a circus\nis for a 12 year old boy.\nLast night we had dinner with some old friends at the Jai\nLai.\nIt was a wonderful dinner served way up high with the games\ngoing on down below and a boy standing at the elbow to place your\nbets.\nDebby didn't do so well because she wasn't cuite as scientific\nas I. I bet on a bounding Basque named Pavlo, because his name re-\nminded me of that dreadful stuff which our girls feed to their unsus-\npecting, trustful babies. He not only won but he was a long shot,\nso I ceme out ahead on the evening by a few paltry pesos.\nI had two business objectives in Manila, neither of which\nhas been wholly attained or completely lost.\nFurthermore, that status\nmay obtain when we leave but at least I've done my best end each\nsituation is at least clarified if nothing more.\nFurthermore, nothing\ncould be accomplished by staying longer.\nWill try to write again from somewhere along the line.\nAll the best,\nH. M. B.",
